  Content: A country within the North Armican continent. Early humans first migrated
    to the continent 12,000 years ago across the Bering land bridge. From the early
    16th century on, various nations colonized parts of the continent (including the
    Spanish, French, and British, to name a few). This would eventually lead to a
    revolution by the colonies of Armica against their ruling monarchies, resulting
    in the formation of the sovereign nation of Armica.
